  "generated_text": "Given the function \\( f(x) \\) defined for all positive real numbers, we know \\( f(x) > 0 \\) for all \\( x > 0 \\). We are also given the functional equation:\n\\[ f(x - y) = \\sqrt{f(xy) + 2} \\]\nfor all \\( x > y > 0 \\).\n\nFirst, let's set \\( x = y \\) in the functional equation:\n\\[ f(0) = \\sqrt{f(y^2) + 2} \\]\n\nSince \\( f(x) > 0 \\) for all \\( x > 0 \\), we can square both sides of the equation:\n\\[ f(0)^2 = f(y^2) + 2 \\]\n\\[ 2 = f(y^2) + 2 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( f(y^2) \\):\n\\[ f(y^2) = 0 \\]\n\nThus, \\( f(x) = 0 \\) for all \\( x > 0 \\).\n\nTherefore:\n\\[ f(2009) = 0 \\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\\[ \\boxed{0} \\]",
